panfrost: submit the JM job bag merged, by default

The kbase JM queue has two submission paths: one job bag per batch, and one
job bag for the whole submit.  The merged path already existed but was gated
behind PANVK_MERGE_SUBMIT, so a default build took the per-batch path, which
submits and waits for every batch in turn.

The per-batch path pays the submit ioctl, the wait ioctl and the wake-up round
trip for every batch, and blocks the CPU behind the GPU each time.  The merged
path keeps the same ordering and the same "waited before returning" lifetime,
and only collapses those round trips.

Ordering and lifetime do not change: the merged bag still declares a linear
data dependency between atoms, and the submit still waits for the whole bag
before returning.  Only the number of submit/wait round trips changes, and a
bag is capped at PANVK_KBASE_JM_MERGE_MAX_BATCHES so the atom numbers stay
below the 256 the wait path tracks.

The benefit is fewer submit/wait round trips and less CPU blocking, not clock
behaviour: on the target device the GPU ramps to its 886 MHz maximum on its own
within ~500 ms under load (measured 2026-11-17, see docs/FAUX123-RE.md).

PANVK_MERGE_SUBMIT=0 restores the per-batch path exactly as it was, for
bisecting a regression.

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_gpu_queue_kbase.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_gpu_queue_kbase.c
index 0f8b1a2..7d2f0c4 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_gpu_queue_kbase.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_gpu_queue_kbase.c
@@ -1560,6 +1560,22 @@
    return VK_SUCCESS;
 }
 
+/* One job bag per submit instead of one bag per batch.  The per-batch path
+ * below submits and waits for every batch, so the CPU round-trips through the
+ * kernel behind the GPU on each one.  The merged path keeps the same ordering
+ * and the same "waited before returning" lifetime, and only collapses the
+ * round trips. */
+static bool
+panvk_merge_submit_enabled(void)
+{
+   static int on = -1;
+   if (on < 0) {
+      const char *e = getenv("PANVK_MERGE_SUBMIT");
+      on = (e && e[0] == '0') ? 0 : 1;
+   }
+   return on != 0;
+}
+
 VkResult
